From 13c806178f3033098dbd85f4dec8bc5b7150ac2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:57:30 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Draw the 3D view with QOpenGLWidget so that it works on
 Wayland

QGLWidget needs a native window of its own, which Qt's Wayland platform
plugins do not give it: on a native Wayland session the 3D view's area stayed
the window's background colour and nothing was logged (measured with Qt 5.15.19
and KWin 6.7 on Mesa 26.1). QOpenGLWidget, available since Qt 5.4, renders
into a framebuffer object and draws on every platform plugin.

The OpenGL calls stay as they were (fixed function, as before). Changes:
QOpenGLWidget as the base class, update() for updateGL(), grabFramebuffer()
for grabFrameBuffer(), glClearColor() for qglClearColor(), QImage's own
RGBA8888 conversion for convertToGLFormat(), the context's getProcAddress()
for glLockArraysEXT, and the 3D View action is enabled when an OpenGL context
can be made, which is what QGLFormat::hasOpenGL() asked.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
